1
00:00:00,640 --> 00:00:01,680
Matthew 11

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:05,980
When Jesus had finished instructing his twelve disciples,

3
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:09,000
he went on from there to teach and preach in their cities.

4
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:12,880
Now when John heard in prison about the deeds of the Christ,

5
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:16,160
he sent word by his disciples and said to him,

6
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,740
Are you the one who is to come, or shall we look for another?

7
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,960
And Jesus answered them,

8
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:25,600
Go, and tell John what you hear and see.

9
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:29,180
The blind receive their sight, and the lame walk.

10
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:33,540
Look, lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, and the dead are raised up,

11
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:36,840
and the poor have good news preached to them.

12
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:40,720
And blessed is the one who is not offended by me.

13
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:45,780
As they went away, Jesus began to speak to the crowds concerning John.

14
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,140
What did you go out into the wilderness to see?

15
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,500
A reed shaken by the wind.

16
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:54,200
What then did you go out to see?

17
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:56,460
A man dressed in soft clothing?

18
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:58,060
Behold,

19
00:00:58,300 --> 00:00:59,160
those who were in the wilderness,

20
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:01,340
those who wear soft clothing are in kings' houses.

21
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,240
What then did you go out to see?

22
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,300
A prophet?

23
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:08,760
Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet.

24
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:11,340
This is he of whom it is written,

25
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:15,880
Behold, I send my messenger before your face,

26
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:18,580
who will prepare your way before you.

27
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,840
Truly I say to you,

28
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,780
among those born of women,

29
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,940
there has arisen no one greater than John the Baptist.

30
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:29,140
Yet the one who is least in the kingdom of heaven,

31
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:30,740
is greater than he.

32
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:34,120
From the days of John the Baptist until now,

33
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,160
the kingdom of heaven has suffered violence,

34
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,100
and the violent take it by force.

35
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:43,120
For all the prophets in the law prophesied until John.

36
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,900
And if you are willing to accept it,

37
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:48,740
he is Elijah who is to come.

38
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:51,500
He who has ears to hear,

39
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:53,000
let him hear.

40
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,160
But to what shall I compare this generation?

41
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:57,800
To this generation.

42
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,940
It is like children sitting in the marketplaces,

43
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:04,060
and calling to their playmates.

44
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:06,300
We played the flute for you,

45
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,860
and you did not dance.

46
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,860
We sing a dirge, and you did not mourn.

47
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,860
For John came neither eating nor drinking,

48
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,020
and they say,

49
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:16,600
He has a demon.

50
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:19,460
The Son of Man came eating and drinking,

51
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:20,220
and they say,

52
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:21,760
Look at him,

53
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,940
a glutton and a drunkard,

54
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:26,900
a friend of tax collectors and sinners.

55
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,080
Yet,

56
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:32,460
his wisdom is justified by her deeds.

57
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:37,160
Then he began to denounce the cities where most of his mighty works had been done,

58
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,160
because they did not repent.

59
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:41,160
Woe to you, Chorazin!

60
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,160
Woe to you, Bethsaida!

61
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:49,160
For if the mighty works done in you had been done in Tyre and Sidon,

62
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:54,160
they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes.

63
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:56,160
But I tell you,

64
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:59,160
it will be more bearable on the day of judgment,

65
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:01,160
for Tyre and Sidon,

66
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:03,160
than for you.

67
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:05,160
And you, Capernaum,

68
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:07,160
will you be exalted to heaven?

69
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:11,160
You will be brought down to Hades.

70
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,160
For if the mighty works done in you

71
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:15,160
had been done in Sodom,

72
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:17,160
it would have remained until this day.

73
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:19,160
But I tell you,

74
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:21,160
that it will be more tolerable on the day of judgment

75
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:23,160
for the land of Sodom,

76
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,160
than for you.

77
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,160
At that time Jesus declared,

78
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,160
I thank you, Father,

79
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:31,160
Lord of heaven and earth,

80
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:33,160
that you have hidden these things

81
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:35,160
from the wise and understanding,

82
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:37,160
and revealed them to little children.

83
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:39,160
Yes, Father,

84
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:41,160
for such was your gracious will.

85
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:43,160
All things have been handed over

86
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:45,160
to me by my Father,

87
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:47,160
and no one knows the Son except the Father,

88
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:49,160
and no one knows the Father

89
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:51,160
except the Son,

90
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:53,160
and anyone to whom the Son

91
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:55,160
chooses to reveal him.

92
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,160
Come to me,

93
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,160
all who labor

94
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,160
and are heavy laden,

95
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,160
and I will give you rest.

96
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,160
Take my yoke upon you,

97
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:07,160
and learn from me,

98
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:09,160
for I am gentle and lowly in heart,

99
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:11,160
and you will find rest

100
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,160
for your souls.

101
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,160
For my yoke is easy,

102
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,160
and my burden is light.

